    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (75.01) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Mathews, where park factors and platoon advantages elevate his floor, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** finds himself in an excellent spot against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez, buoyed by a 14% boost from his dynamic platoon splits and a locked-in #2 spot in the order. **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) and **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) also rate as elite starts today; **Jacob Wilson** is primed to exploit a hitter-friendly environment, and **Cole Carrigg** remains a high-value play because of his switch-hitting versatility and the favorable matchup against Luinder Avila, which allows him to capitalize on his elite sprint speed\u2014a critical asset for our 5x5 Roto standing.\n\nWhile the optimizer is aggressive with our primary starters, **Gunnar Henderson** (53.01) represents our toughest bench decision. Despite his pedigree, the combination of a daunting matchup against the talented Cristopher S\u00e1nchez and significant platoon degradation pushed him just below the threshold for a starting spot today. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on the 37% rain risk impacting our Cardinals and Braves matchups. Should the weather hold, **Drake Baldwin** (69.59) is set up for a massive day against Miles Mikolas, provided he confirms his #2 spot in the lineup. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Coby Mayo** (56.20); while the wind-out conditions at his home park offer a power boost, he faces a stiff test in Cristopher S\u00e1nchez, which necessitated a slight downward adjustment to his expectation despite his strong plate positioning. \n\nThe lineup will remain balanced, but we are effectively sacrificing the upside of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Sam Antonacci** to prioritize the daily efficiency and current matchup favorability of the aforementioned group. We will continue to monitor the status of **Drake Baldwin**, **Dominic Smith**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Cole Carrigg**, as all carry \"Lineup Pending\" status; if any of these players are dropped from their respective lineups, we will pivot to our depth reserves, including **Luis Lara** or **Denzer Guzman**, to ensure our lineup remains optimized for the 5x5 categories.",
